    <node id="CVE-2015-8871">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Use-after-free in opj_j2k_write_mco</data>
      <data key="d3">Hi,

I have found a potential use-after-free in opj_j2k_write_mco function, of the [j2k.c](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5545) file.

At line [5562](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5562), l_current_data is set to p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data.
But at line [5567](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5567), p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data is used as arg of realloc, and so can be freed.

But  l_current_data is used later (line [5597](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5597), [5582](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5582) ...), and so can point to a freed memory zone

A simple fixed, should be to affect l_current_data to p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data after the line [5577](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5577)

The vulnerability was found by my static binary analyzer gueb (that will become open-source soon)

Regards,
Feist Josselin
</data>
    </node>
    <node id="uclouvain/openjpeg#563">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Use-after-free in opj_j2k_write_mco</data>
      <data key="d3">Hi,

I have found a potential use-after-free in opj_j2k_write_mco function, of the [j2k.c](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5545) file.

At line [5562](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5562), l_current_data is set to p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data.
But at line [5567](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5567), p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data is used as arg of realloc, and so can be freed.

But  l_current_data is used later (line [5597](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5597), [5582](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5582) ...), and so can point to a freed memory zone

A simple fixed, should be to affect l_current_data to p_j2k-&gt;m_specific_param.m_encoder.m_header_tile_data after the line [5577](https://github.com/uclouvain/openjpeg/blob/master/src/lib/openjp2/j2k.c#L5577)

The vulnerability was found by my static binary analyzer gueb (that will become open-source soon)

Regards,
Feist Josselin
</data>
