    <node id="CVE-2016-2145">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Segmentation Fault</data>
      <data key="d3">I've stumbled across a Segmentation Fault in mod_auth_mellon.so (v. 0.9.1) running on httpd-2.4.6-31.el7.x86_64. I ran the program through gdb for more information, but unfortunately I don't have debugging symbols for mod_auth_mellon. Here is the backtrace:

```
(gdb) backtrace full
#0  0x00007fc3debccf81 in apr_brigade_create () from /lib64/libaprutil-1.so.0
#1  0x00007fc3df4eda55 in ap_get_client_block ()
#2  0x00007fc3d0ff9342 in am_read_post_data () from /etc/httpd/modules/mod_auth_mellon.so
#3  0x00007fc3d0ffe6ce in am_handler () from /etc/httpd/modules/mod_auth_mellon.so
#4  0x00007fc3df4d4d70 in ap_run_handler ()
#5  0x00007fc3df4d52b9 in ap_invoke_handler ()
#6  0x00007fc3df4e963a in ap_process_async_request ()
#7  0x00007fc3df4e9914 in ap_process_request ()
#8  0x00007fc3df4e62a2 in ap_process_http_connection ()
#9  0x00007fc3df4de340 in ap_run_process_connection ()
#10 0x00007fc3d4eaf80f in child_main () from /etc/httpd/modules/mod_mpm_prefork.so
#11 0x00007fc3d4eafa55 in make_child () from /etc/httpd/modules/mod_mpm_prefork.so
#12 0x00007fc3d4eb06ee in prefork_run () from /etc/httpd/modules/mod_mpm_prefork.so
#13 0x00007fc3df4bb2ce in ap_run_mpm ()
#14 0x00007fc3df4b48f6 in main ()
```

This is noticeable to the end user. When the IDP is redirecting (HTTP 303) back to the SP (using mod_auth_mellon) with a postResponse, there is a 30-50 second stall, after which the user has a "valid" SAML session. 

This error occurs in the most recent version of IE 11 and Chrome, but not in Firefox (or when proxying traffic through Fiddler).
</data>
    </node>
