    <node id="CVE-2016-6250">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Integer overflow checking filename size for ISO9660</data>
      <data key="d3">Reported by: Christian Wressnegger, Alwin Maier, and Fabian Yamaguchi

The ISO9660 writer is subject to integer overflows when verifying the filename size.  This can lead to a crash when writing ISO9660 images with 2GB or 4GB filenames.
</data>
