    <node id="marcobambini/gravity#130">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Stack Overflow (operator_int_cmp) </data>
      <data key="d3">There is a stack based buffer overflow in the operator_int_cmp function. By using the testcase below, it is possible to trigger a stack overflow. It has something to do with the "self" value being called. Attached is the valgrind, ASAN, and GDB output. 

```
class Crash
{
	var x,y,w,h;
	
	func init (n1,n2,n3,n4)
	{
		x = n1;
		y = n2;
		w = n3;
		h = n4;
	}
	
	func Int()
	{	
		var i;

		while (i &lt; self)
		{
			i += 1;
		}

		return i+i;
	}
}


func main()
{
	var a = 10;
	var b = Crash(1,2,3,4);
	return a + b;
}
</data>
