    <node id="CVE-2017-1000498">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">XXE DoS within SVG Parsing</data>
      <data key="d3"># Issue
androidsvg is vulnerable to XXE attacks as some dangerous features are not disabled. This leads to a confirmed denial of service scenario (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billion_laughs_attack) and may lead to execution of commands on the server.

This issue occurs in the SVG parse section of the code:
https://github.com/BigBadaboom/androidsvg/blob/1f53713100a0e3e30bb3b29308588fc2ea41b06d/androidsvg/src/main/java/com/caverock/androidsvg/SVGParser.java#L576

Prior to parsing the XML, features like entities are not disabled. These should not be required at all within an SVG file.
https://github.com/BigBadaboom/androidsvg/blob/1f53713100a0e3e30bb3b29308588fc2ea41b06d/androidsvg/src/main/java/com/caverock/androidsvg/SVGParser.java#L606

# Remediation
Implementing something down the lines of the following:
```Java
SAXParserFactory spf = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
spf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);
```
This ensures that the entities are no longer parsed and external dtd files are not either.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BigBadaboom/androidsvg#122">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">XXE DoS within SVG Parsing</data>
      <data key="d3"># Issue
androidsvg is vulnerable to XXE attacks as some dangerous features are not disabled. This leads to a confirmed denial of service scenario (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billion_laughs_attack) and may lead to execution of commands on the server.

This issue occurs in the SVG parse section of the code:
https://github.com/BigBadaboom/androidsvg/blob/1f53713100a0e3e30bb3b29308588fc2ea41b06d/androidsvg/src/main/java/com/caverock/androidsvg/SVGParser.java#L576

Prior to parsing the XML, features like entities are not disabled. These should not be required at all within an SVG file.
https://github.com/BigBadaboom/androidsvg/blob/1f53713100a0e3e30bb3b29308588fc2ea41b06d/androidsvg/src/main/java/com/caverock/androidsvg/SVGParser.java#L606

# Remediation
Implementing something down the lines of the following:
```Java
SAXParserFactory spf = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
spf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
spf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);
```
This ensures that the entities are no longer parsed and external dtd files are not either.</data>
