    <node id="CVE-2017-16017">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">XSS injection vulnerability using empty, undelimited attributes</data>
      <data key="d3">Entering the following:

``` html
&lt;IMG SRC= onmouseover="alert('XSS');"&gt;
```

produces the following:

``` html
&lt;img src="onmouseover="alert('XSS');"" /&gt;
```

This is definitely invalid HTML, but would suggest that it's being interpreted incorrectly by the parser. I would expect:

``` html
&lt;img src="" /&gt;
```
</data>
    </node>
    <node id="apostrophecms/sanitize-html#19">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">XSS injection vulnerability using empty, undelimited attributes</data>
      <data key="d3">Entering the following:

``` html
&lt;IMG SRC= onmouseover="alert('XSS');"&gt;
```

produces the following:

``` html
&lt;img src="onmouseover="alert('XSS');"" /&gt;
```

This is definitely invalid HTML, but would suggest that it's being interpreted incorrectly by the parser. I would expect:

``` html
&lt;img src="" /&gt;
```
</data>
