    <node id="CVE-2017-16038">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">Directory Traversal</data>
      <data key="d3">First of all, this is an awesome package with lots of functionalities. 

It just has a directory traversal issue, which can be fixed by adding some filtering on the requested url path. To exploit the vulnerability, I can just send a web request say: ```http://localhost:80/../../../``` to browse and retrieve any file on the hosting server.

Notice: the above url does not work with ```wget``` or a browser. Try it by using ```http.get``` in a Node.js program.</data>
    </node>
