      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Segmentation faults in mime handling</data>
      <data key="d3">Hello,
I was using American Fuzzy Lop (afl-fuzz) to fuzz input to the mime-parse test program. Is fixing these crashes something you're interested in? The input files can be found here: https://github.com/rwhitworth/libetpan-fuzz/.

The files can be executed as `./mime-parse id_filename` to cause seg faults.

Let me know if I can provide any more information to help narrow down this issue.</data>
