    <node id="Yeraze/ytnef#48">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">overread of heap-data in TNEFDefaultHandler by a  missing null byte</data>
      <data key="d3">We find the following code may cause over-read of buffer and leak extra bytes to the output.
The reason is that the `data` char array is user controlled value and not guaranteed to end with a '\0' byte. So it needs extra checking or we can  force the last byte to be '\0'.
```
libytnef.c: 246
int TNEFDefaultHandler STD_ARGLIST {
  if (TNEF-&gt;Debug &gt;= 1){ 
+          data[size-1]='\0';
    printf("%s: [%i] %s\n", TNEFList[id].name, size, data);}
  return 0;
}

```
The un-patched code running with the testcase proving the problem.
[testcase](https://github.com/bingosxs/fuzzdata/raw/master/ytnef-1.9/18-TNEFDefaultHandler.tnef)

the tracelog is;
```

