    <node id="CVE-2018-19115">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">http healthcheck may be received an unexpected response and cause memory access violation in extract_status_code</data>
      <data key="d3">when http server response an unexpected response during http healthcheck, for example:
"aa aaaaaaaaaaaHTTP/1.1aa200aaaaaaaaaaOKaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa..........."

then, strncat will cause memory  corrupted in extract_status_code, due to inc++  is increasing to a large value ( &gt; 10 ).

https://github.com/acassen/keepalived/blob/master/lib/html.c:
	while (buffer &lt; end &amp;&amp; *buffer++ != ' ')
		inc++;
	strncat(buf_code, begin, inc);

but, buf_code has only 10 bytes. 

this is 100% reproduced.

</data>
