    <node id="CVE-2018-20652">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d2">Out of Memory in function tinyexr::ReadAttribute in tinyexr.h</data>
      <data key="d3">Hi, there.

An Out of Memory problem was discovered in function tinyexr::ReadAttribute in tinyexr.h. The program tries to allocate with a large number size( 0xffffffffd6bb0049 bytes) of memory.

Please use the "./test_tinyexr $POC" to reproduce the bug.
[POC.zip](https://github.com/syoyo/tinyexr/files/2718192/POC.zip)


The ASAN dumps the stack trace of POC1 as follows:

```
==368==ERROR: AddressSanitizer failed to allocate 0xffffffffd6bb0049 bytes
==368==AddressSanitizer's allocator is terminating the process instead of returning 0
==368==AddressSanitizer CHECK failed: /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_allocator.cc:225 "((0)) != (0)" (0x0, 0x0)
    #0 0x4e4895 in __asan::AsanCheckFailed(char const*, int, char const*, unsigned long long, unsigned long long) /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_rtl.cc:69
    #1 0x502155 in __sanitizer::CheckFailed(char const*, int, char const*, unsigned long long, unsigned long long) /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_termination.cc:79
    #2 0x4eac96 in __sanitizer::ReportAllocatorCannotReturnNull() /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_allocator.cc:225
    #3 0x4ead1f in __sanitizer::DieOnFailure::OnOOM() /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_allocator.cc:257
    #4 0x513e24 in operator new(unsigned long) /llvm-6.0.1/projects/compiler-rt/lib/asan/asan_new_delete.cc:92
    #5 0x564360 in __gnu_cxx::new_allocator&lt;unsigned char&gt;::allocate(unsigned long, void const*) /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7.3.0/../../../../include/c++/7.3.0/ext/new_allocator.h:111:27
    #6 0x56424e in std::allocator_traits&lt;std::allocator&lt;unsigned char&gt; &gt;::allocate(std::allocator&lt;unsigned char&gt;&amp;, unsigned long) /usr/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-gnu/7.3.0/../../../../include/c++/7.3.0/bits/alloc_traits.h:436:20
    #7 0x56365f in std::_Vector_base&lt;unsigned char, std::allocator&lt;unsigned char&gt; &gt;::_M_allocate(unsigned long) /usr/lib/</data>
    </node>
