    <node id="CVE-2018-6353">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">python</data>
      <data key="d2">why is it possible to execute arbitrary system commands via python code through the electrum (Qt) console</data>
      <data key="d3">wondering why it is currently possible to execute arbitrary system commands via python code through the electrum console, and why there is no whitelisting/blacklisting of allowed methods/functions as this seems like a major security issue
  
inserting a payload such as below in the console, then checking /tmp for the file creation shows the file was successfully created
&gt;&gt; lol=__import__('os');lol.system('/bin/sh -c "touch /tmp/test"');print(lol.path.isfile('/tmp/test')); 
True</data>
    </node>
    <node id="spesmilo/electrum#3678">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">why is it possible to execute arbitrary system commands via python code through the electrum (Qt) console</data>
      <data key="d3">wondering why it is currently possible to execute arbitrary system commands via python code through the electrum console, and why there is no whitelisting/blacklisting of allowed methods/functions as this seems like a major security issue
  
inserting a payload such as below in the console, then checking /tmp for the file creation shows the file was successfully created
&gt;&gt; lol=__import__('os');lol.system('/bin/sh -c "touch /tmp/test"');print(lol.path.isfile('/tmp/test')); 
True</data>
