    <node id="CVE-2019-15499">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">Open Redirect / XSS via iframe with sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">## Summary
This is similar issue to #959, but different cause.
Due to `sandbox` attribute is allowed, attacker can redirect victim to something malicious if attacker embeds iframe with `allow-top-navigation` in `sandbox` attribute. 
#959 won't work in Chrome because of their security, but this will work due to `sandbox` is whitelist attribute.
This will be XSS in Safari by using data scheme.
## Step to reproduce
1. Type ```&lt;iframe src="https://example.com/hackmd.html" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-top-navigation allow-scripts"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;``` in Editor. (It doesn't work because my domain is expired.)
2. View edited page.

[PoC](https://demo.codimd.org/YcIX0oKzQAuZMMOqxeASdg)
(This PoC will redirect you to [example.com](https://example.com))

## CVE
[CVE-2019-15499](https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2019-15499)

## Suggested fix
Don't allow `sandbox` attribute in public/js/render.js.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="hackmdio/codimd#1263">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Open Redirect / XSS via iframe with sandbox.</data>
      <data key="d3">## Summary
This is similar issue to #959, but different cause.
Due to `sandbox` attribute is allowed, attacker can redirect victim to something malicious if attacker embeds iframe with `allow-top-navigation` in `sandbox` attribute. 
#959 won't work in Chrome because of their security, but this will work due to `sandbox` is whitelist attribute.
This will be XSS in Safari by using data scheme.
## Step to reproduce
1. Type ```&lt;iframe src="https://example.com/hackmd.html" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-top-navigation allow-scripts"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;``` in Editor. (It doesn't work because my domain is expired.)
2. View edited page.

[PoC](https://demo.codimd.org/YcIX0oKzQAuZMMOqxeASdg)
(This PoC will redirect you to [example.com](https://example.com))

## CVE
[CVE-2019-15499](https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2019-15499)

## Suggested fix
Don't allow `sandbox` attribute in public/js/render.js.</data>
      <data key="d4">[]</data>
