    <node id="CVE-2020-13881">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Printing server secret key in plain text in journalctl</data>
      <data key="d3">In the example, we can see that server secret key is printed in plain text in journalctl logs. If an attacker is using man-in-the-middle attack and somehow gets these logs, he/she can decrypt and see all packets. User passwords will also be exposed by that.</data>
    </node>
