    <node id="kjur/jsrsasign#442">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Generated RSA keys do not always have requested length</data>
      <data key="d3">I'm using the following code to generate RSA keys:
```
node@nodejs /u/h/node&gt; cat test/generate-key.js
#!/usr/bin/env node

jsrsasign = require('jsrsasign');

var rsaDespair = jsrsasign.KEYUTIL.generateKeypair('RSA', 2048);
var pem = jsrsasign.KEYUTIL.getPEM(rsaDespair.prvKeyObj, 'PKCS1PRV');
console.log(pem);
```

Sometimes the generated key has less than 2048 bits:
```
node@nodejs /u/h/node&gt; while test/generate-key.js | tee broken.key | openssl rsa -noout -text | grep 2048; end; cat broken.key
