    <node id="CVE-2020-22783">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">Etherpad lite stores admin/user password in plain-text in the log file and in the database </data>
      <data key="d3">Hello,

With loglevel DEBUG and INFO Etherpad lite stores the admin/user password - f.i. to access ~/etherpad-lite/admin/pluguns - in plain-text in the log file.

And in every loglevel Etherpad lite stores these admin/user password in plain-text in the database Etherpad lite.

Is there a way to avoid it for security reason?

Greetings &amp; Thanks,
Michael
</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ether/etherpad-lite#2216">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Etherpad lite stores admin/user password in plain-text in the log file and in the database </data>
