    <node id="CVE-2020-25756">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">A buffer overflow error in mg_get_http_header</data>
      <data key="d3">A buffer overflow error in mg_get_http_header function in mongoose/src/mg_http.c in Mongoose 6.18, where header_names and header_values have a bound of (MG_MAX_HTTP_HEADERS); however, there is no check to ensure that the loop does not exceed the upper bound. A Maliciously crafted  http header can trigger this bug. To fix it, modify the loop condition into:
   
 for (i = 0;i &lt; MG_MAX_HTTP_HEADERS &amp;&amp; hm-&gt;header_names[i].len &gt; 0  ; i++)  </data>
    </node>
    <node id="cesanta/mongoose#1135">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">A buffer overflow error in mg_get_http_header</data>
      <data key="d3">A buffer overflow error in mg_get_http_header function in mongoose/src/mg_http.c in Mongoose 6.18, where header_names and header_values have a bound of (MG_MAX_HTTP_HEADERS); however, there is no check to ensure that the loop does not exceed the upper bound. A Maliciously crafted  http header can trigger this bug. To fix it, modify the loop condition into:
   
 for (i = 0;i &lt; MG_MAX_HTTP_HEADERS &amp;&amp; hm-&gt;header_names[i].len &gt; 0  ; i++)  </data>
