    <node id="CVE-2020-7690">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">XSS vulnerability in html method</data>
      <data key="d3">When using the html method, it is possible to inject code that is executed in the user context. E.g. like this:
```js
const doc = new jsPDF();
window.html2canvas = html2canvas;
const html = `
&lt;p id='test'&gt;a&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=x onerror=eval("document.getElementById('test').innerHTML=window.location") /&gt;
`;
doc.html(html, {
  callback: function (doc) {
    doc.save();
  }
});
```

E.g., this line seems to be suspicious: https://github.com/MrRio/jsPDF/blob/master/src/modules/html.js#L52.

We need to analyze how to fix this and if there is other vulnerable code.</data>
    </node>
    <node id="parallax/jsPDF#2795">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">XSS vulnerability in html method</data>
      <data key="d3">When using the html method, it is possible to inject code that is executed in the user context. E.g. like this:
```js
const doc = new jsPDF();
window.html2canvas = html2canvas;
const html = `
&lt;p id='test'&gt;a&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;img src=x onerror=eval("document.getElementById('test').innerHTML=window.location") /&gt;
`;
doc.html(html, {
  callback: function (doc) {
    doc.save();
  }
});
```

E.g., this line seems to be suspicious: https://github.com/MrRio/jsPDF/blob/master/src/modules/html.js#L52.

We need to analyze how to fix this and if there is other vulnerable code.</data>
      <data key="d4">[]</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
