    <node id="CVE-2021-20245">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">c</data>
      <data key="d2">Division by zero in WriteAnimatedWEBPImage() in coders/webp.c </data>
      <data key="d3">When `image-&gt;ticks_per_second` was set to zero, a division by zero error would happen in line 961. So a crafted file may trigger undefined behavior in the form of division by zero. Maybe there need a `PerceptibleReciprocal()` to do division in line 961?

https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/blob/74f8868c779a5bde13f594ae12955d5d281ef890/coders/webp.c#L936-L967</data>
    </node>
