      <data key="d3">Squashfs stores the filename in the directory entry, this is then used by `unsquashfs` to create the new file during the unsquash. The filename is not validated for traversal outside of the destination directory, this allows writing to locations outside of the destination, such as `/etc/crontab` which could lead to code execution.

To test this, the following change can be made to `mksquashfs`: https://gist.github.com/staaldraad/6799182a78410081238e75d5abec2da0#file-mksquashfs-patch

```
--- mksquashfs.org      2019-09-10 16:11:21.000000000 +0200
+++ mksquashfs.c        2019-09-10 16:12:28.000000000 +0200
@@ -3168,8 +3168,15 @@
