    <node id="CVE-2016-1000237">
      <data key="d0">CVE</data>
      <data key="d1">javascript</data>
      <data key="d2">Sanitization not applied recursively</data>
      <data key="d3">Sanitization is not applied recursively, leading to a vulnerability to certain masking attacks. Example:

`I am not harmless: &lt;&lt;img src="csrf-attack"/&gt;img src="csrf-attack"/&gt;` is sanitized to `I am not harmless: &lt;img src="csrf-attack"/&gt;`

Mitigation: Run sanitization recursively until the input html matches the output html.
</data>
    </node>
